        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "REMUNERATION POLICY OF TATA TECHNOLOGIES LIMITED FOR DIRECTORS, KEY MANAGERIAL PERSONNEL AND OTHER EMPLOYEES"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 1
            },
            "bbox": [
                154,
                118,
                841,
                152
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "The philosophy for remuneration of directors, Key Managerial Personnel (“KMP”) and all other employees of Tata Technologies Limited (“the Company”) is based on the commitment of fostering a culture of leadership with trust. The remuneration policy is aligned to this philosophy."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                84,
                158,
                910,
                198
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "This remuneration policy has been prepared pursuant to the provisions of Section 178(3) of the Companies Act, 2013 (“Act”). While formulating this policy, the Nomination and Remuneration Committee (“NRC”) has considered the factors laid down under Section 178(4) of the Act, which are as under:"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                84,
                204,
                910,
                242
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "(a) the level and composition of remuneration is reasonable and suficient to attract, retain and motivate directors of the quality required to run the company successfully;"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                85,
                249,
                910,
                276
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "(b) relationship of remuneration to performance is clear and meets appropriate performance benchmarks; and"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                85,
                281,
                769,
                295
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "(c) remuneration to directors, key managerial personnel and senior management involves a balance between fixed and incentive pay reflecting short and long-term performance objectives appropriate to the working of the company and its goals."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                85,
                302,
                910,
                329
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Key principles governing this remuneration policy are as follows:"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                85,
                334,
                476,
                348
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Remuneration for independent directors and non-independent non- executive directors"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                85,
                355,
                617,
                369
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Independent directors (“ID”) and non-independent non-executive directors (“NED”) may be paid sitting fees (for attending the meetings of the Board and of committees of which they may be members). In addition to the sitting fees, ID may be paid commission within regulatory limits."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                85,
                374,
                912,
                414
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Within the parameters prescribed by law, the payment of sitting fees and commission will be recommended by the NRC and approved by the Board."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                85,
                419,
                910,
                445
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
